claimed: idiomatic-api-compare — replace the forced chunkSize=1 comparison (methodologically off: it named an artificial mode, not either library's real API) with what each library's OWN idiomatic surface offers, verified from zio-streams' actual sources (not memory): ZStream.fromIterable(list) for sending a collection (DefaultChunkSize=4096), ZStream.unfold(s)(f) for an effectful step-by-step generator (verified: Chunk.single(a) per step, ZIO's real per-element path, not an imposed one), runForeach for element-at-a-time consumption (verified: ZSink.foreach over the same chunk machinery), runCollect/runFold for whole-stream. Mirror each with okay's most efficient equivalent (Source.of, Source.range, Drain-based read, toLazyList.foldLeft) and measure the four axes pairwise rather than one blended "elementwise" row.
